Lab 3: Create Virtual Machine Instances (VMIs)
Lab Overview
This lab focuses on creating and managing Virtual Machine Instances (VMIs) using OpenShift Virtualization. You will learn to define VM specifications through YAML manifests, configure resource allocations, and monitor VM lifecycle operations.

Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

Create Virtual Machine Instances (VMIs) using YAML manifests
Configure CPU, memory, and storage specifications for VMs
Deploy VMIs on OpenShift clusters
Monitor and manage VM lifecycle operations
Troubleshoot common VMI deployment issues
Understand the relationship between VMIs and OpenShift resources
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, ensure you have:

Basic understanding of Kubernetes/OpenShift concepts (pods, deployments, services)
Familiarity with YAML syntax and structure
Knowledge of Linux command-line operations
Understanding of virtualization concepts
Access to OpenShift CLI (oc) commands
Basic networking knowledge
